INT. TAXIDERMY AUCTION HOUSE - BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Shelves of glass-eyed animals line the walls: a bear, a pheasant, a snarling badger mounted on a plinth. Tags dangle from their feet. A single green-shaded lamp. A card table with a briefcase on it.

LUCIAN VARGA, 40s, silk scarf, silver rings, leans on the table. DOMINIC ACHEBE, 30s, broad-shouldered in a gray suit, stands in the doorway, arms folded. Between them sits ROSALIND BEAUMONT, 50s, an auctioneer's apron over her blouse, hands flat on the briefcase.

LUCIAN
Open it.

ROSALIND
I told you. The lot is withdrawn.

LUCIAN
Open it, Rosalind.

She does not. Dominic pushes off the doorframe. He walks to the bear, runs a hand down its flank, and puts his thumb through a seam in the hide. He pulls it wider. Stuffing spills out. So do three small velvet pouches, which drop to the floor and clink. Rosalind flinches. Lucian smiles like a man who is bored by being right.

DOMINIC
Found something.

ROSALIND
Please don't.

Dominic crouches and picks up a pouch. He loosens its drawstring and pours a dozen uncut stones into his palm, cloudy, gray, ugly. He looks at Lucian. Lucian looks at Rosalind. She puts her face in her hands.

LUCIAN
Where's the rest?

ROSALIND
That's all of it.

LUCIAN
That's not ten million.

ROSALIND
The rest is in the badger.

Dominic stands, crosses to the badger, and grips it by the scruff. The plinth wobbles. He lifts it. Something rattles inside.

A door bangs open at the far end of the room. TOBIAS FINCH, 20s, a young constable in a damp uniform, steps in with a flashlight in one hand and a radio clipped to his shoulder. He freezes. The flashlight beam finds Dominic holding the badger, Lucian leaning on the table, Rosalind with her face in her hands.

TOBIAS
Evening. Everything all right in here?

LUCIAN
Perfectly, officer.

TOBIAS
Door was open.

LUCIAN
We're appraising.

TOBIAS
At eleven at night?

DOMINIC
(a beat)
Estate sale.

Tobias looks at the bear. At the spilled stuffing. At the pouches on the floor. His flashlight drifts to the badger and then up to Dominic's face. He sniffs.

TOBIAS
That's an interesting badger.

Nobody breathes. The badger rattles again as Dominic's grip shifts.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
My nan had one.

LUCIAN
(carefully)
Did she?

TOBIAS
Tore it up when I was seven. I wanted to see inside.

ROSALIND
(muffled)
What did you find?

TOBIAS
Sawdust. And a hundred pounds.

A long, strange quiet. Lucian laughs, one abrupt breath. Dominic sets down the badger very slowly. Rosalind lowers her hands. Tobias holds up the flashlight and clicks it off.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
I'll say the door was locked.

He leaves. His footsteps recede down the corridor. Lucian walks to the pouches and starts gathering them. Dominic watches the empty doorway.
